WEBVTT

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:39.000
Ah, sorry to have borrowed this much from you.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.550
I want to finish reading all of them in one go.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:47.300
It's true that there are many settings in this manga that you can forget easily if not read together.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:53.160
That's right. After you read half of it, you can't tell who the friends and foes are anymore.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:59.310
Me neither. I was so confused when this character who I thought died before volume 40 suddenly reappeared.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.690
Yup, totally!

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.690
What the-? I thought you understood it inside and out.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.690
Eh? Well...

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.450
Fuyuki, which character do you think is the best?

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.900
Um... which character do you prefer, Kana-san?

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.140
The Earl of course!

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.160
Me too.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.430
But that indecisiveness of his is unacceptable.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.670
It gets on my nerves.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.100
Indeed.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:28.070
Let's discuss this after I finish reading, Fuyuki, my friend.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.270
Sure, I'll be glad to.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.710
They're heavy. Let me help you carry them.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:34.650
Nah, I'm fine. No big deal.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.530
Then please be careful.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.890
It's snowing pretty hard...

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:59.190
You came back late today. Did something happen?

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.160
No, not really.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.240
If it's nothing then why were you late?

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.210
That's rare of you.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.930
Is the reason for coming home late that important?

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:10.130
No, not really...

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:14.430
I was taking care of the hamster.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.740
It's only Shuuichi and I who are tending to it.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.590
What the-? That's it? How boring.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:21.570
Hey, you...

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.570
Good afternoon.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.280
Did you borrow that manga from Fuyuki?

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:49.450
Huh? Yeah. That guy is really hardcore to have collected the whole set of this shoujo manga.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:52.150
So is he a noble or of royal blood?

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.300
Do you want to read it, Chiaki?

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:54.370
No.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:58.240
You're not being honest.
Compared to you, Fuyuki is so much nicer.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.300
Why's that?

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:04.360
He addresses me with honorifics.
This shows he respects his seniors.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:08.310
I use honorifics too. It's just that I choose whom to use them with.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.030
That's where you are different, Akechi-kun.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:14.030
That guy would smile and address people with honorifics regardless of who they are.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.320
I'm home!

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:37.430
The snow has really built up. It's really cold outside.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:40.590
Cold weather is the enemy of women.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.140
R–Really?

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.720
Yeah, don't let your guard down.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:45.550
You're joking, right?

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:47.850
There's going to be a rare, huge, snowfall tonight.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.190
What should we have for dinner?

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:50.910
Sushi!

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.650
That's a bit too...

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.700
There isn't much here.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.540
Two frozen gratin, huh.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.470
There's only sliced bread and spaghetti here.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.640
There are only weird ingredients.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:11.540
What should we do?

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:15.540
Let's have nabe with all these ingredients cooked together.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.060
Eh? Yami nabe?

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:18.550
That's impossible.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.310
The gas tank's empty, and it seems we don't have any in storage.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.860
Aw man, we used it all up?

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:27.050
Looks like we'll have to do some shopping.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:34.720
The snow has really built up. It's really cold outside.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.530
Maybe we should just make do with what we have.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:40.020
You're right. Let's do that.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.280
I'll help out, Haruka-neesama.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.750
Then let's start preparing.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:48.360
I'll be reading my manga! Call me when dinner's ready!

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.280
Who do you think you are?

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.180
I'm full. I'm satisfied. I'm delighted. I'm stuffed.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:04.630
My stomach doesn't even have one centimeter of space left.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:08.180
That's true. We pretty much used up all the ingredients that were left.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:12.560
Tomorrow I'll definitely have to go grocery shopping.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.360
If that's the case, please remember to buy this...

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.840
There's only one left.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:21.570
Can you stop by the cleaners on the way? I forgot to bring back my coat.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:24.110
You took it there, so get it yourself.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.070
Ah?

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.790
In any case, let's talk about this tomorrow. It's still snowing.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.330
That's right! Tomorrow! Tomorrow!

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.750
There's no need to go out in this weather.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:40.450
But, our neighbor has just gone to work. I passed by him at the elevator.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.350
What kind of job would that be?

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:44.760
Is that what you're supposed to take a jab at?

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:48.400
Go get your clothes at the cleaners yourself.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.280
I wonder how much snow has accumulated.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.980
Let's go have a look.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:57.200
Oh, there's so much! Everything is all white!

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:00.270
You're right. It's so pretty.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.610
It's really cold. Let's go back inside.

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:18.960
Okay.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:22.520
Cold weather is the enemy of women, after all.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:23.180
Eh?

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:26.530
I'm all set! Let's go out and play!

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:31.030
Eh? Are we really going?

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:37.310
Stop dilly-dallying. The right way to spend a snowy day is to run around the courtyard, having fun.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:40.400
And then cuddle up under the kotatsu? You idiot.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.830
Yay!

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:52.830
That's for spacing out!

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:55.250
Oh, you're getting into the spirit!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.350
Player Kana, making her first pitch!

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.510
Now you've done it, Haruka! Damn it!

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.490
That hurts, geez...

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:18.020
Come on, Chiaki. You're not a kid that would give up so easily.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:20.820
Don't mess with me! I'll make you pay dearly for this!

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.550
Yes! Finished!

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.920
Don't you think this guy looks odd?

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:31.940
A little...

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:36.550
Next, let me teach you what winter sports are all about!

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:38.540
Is there something you're capable of?

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:40.160
Don't be ridden by the snowboard.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:41.170
Ride the snowboard!

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:42.330
You aren't making any sense.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.250
It's about time we head back. It's so cold.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.220
All right! It's almost 'about time' too!

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.660
What're you planning?

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.550
You'll know when we get back.

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:02.730
It might be a bit too hot.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.220
How's this 'about time'?

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:05.960
Sorry for the wait.

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:09.050
You idiot, what's this 'Sorry for the wait'?

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:12.070
Kids who can't appreciate elegance should just step aside.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:12.620
Why you.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:18.440
How's this? This is something you can only experience on a snowy day.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:19.060
Also,

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.780
this feeling of freedom!

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:26.700
It's a bit too cool.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.090
I put in too much snow.

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:29.300
Then heat it up a bit.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:35.010
Soaking like this makes it feel as though it's not our house's tub.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.330
It feels good, don't you think?

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.560
Be quiet. Just get out.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.060
I don't want to.

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:43.600
Move aside, you!

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.340
Don't be so cold.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.780
Let's go out again after a bit of rest.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:51.750
Haven't you had enough?

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.990
No! The second phase of this snowy night has just started.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:10:00.750
It's so relaxing. It's snowing outside and we're sitting under the kotatsu having snacks.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:03.280
Oh? A blackout?

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:05.590
Haruka-neesama.

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:08.010
Don't worry. It's going to be fixed soon.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:37.790
S–So cold...

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:40.790
Do you think it will become warm by saying that?

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:44.140
I'm saying it's cold because it's cold. What's wrong with that?

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:44.730
Like I said...

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:48.300
Now, now, the electricity will be back soon.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:51.250
I hope my body can last until then.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.740
This is bad. I'm feeling sleepy.

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:59.210
Our food supplies are low, and there's no way of contacting outside.

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:01.300
Are we going to die here?

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:09.840
Chiaki. Chiaki. Quick! Say that phrase!

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:13.330
Eh? Oh. There's only 100 million yen.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:16.960
That's not it! What kind of circumstance is that?

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:19.960
Wait, I guess you can after all.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:23.000
It's cold enough already. Can't you just shut up?

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:25.280
Boring!

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:27.250
Where are you going?

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:31.610
The bath. The water should still be warm. I'm going to warm myself up.

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:34.150
There's nothing wrong with bathing in the dark, right?

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:50.090
The water has become cold. And the window is open.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:52.170
Who opened the window?!

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:53.190
You did.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.370
Oh right. Damn, it was me!

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.470
Did you close the window?

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.370
I wasn't in a position to do so.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.690
So cold.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:06.670
Hurry and put on your clothes. You're going to catch a cold.

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:09.250
Haruka-neesama?

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:11.920
I'm going to shut the window.

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:24.250
Hey... you're grossing me out. Stop squeezing it!

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:27.190
I never would have thought this was the only way to get warm.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:32.300
Stop asking for so much. Be glad we even have one left.

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:35.420
I'm hungry. I want to eat something.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:37.090
There is something.

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:40.410
Really?! I'll eat it! I want to eat it! Let's eat it!

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:42.280
It's frozen. Will that do?

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.910
Oh, that!

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:48.250
If we eat that, we'd get frozen from the inside.

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.560
If only we could heat up some water...

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:54.490
Impossible. There's no gas.

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:56.180
Darn...

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:01.980
If we mix wheat flour with water and eggs, will it taste like hot cakes?

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.390
I'll help you make it.

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:06.720
No... forget it.

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:26.430
This isn't funny. Is the power back yet?

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:29.400
They sure are taking a long time to fix it.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:34.580
Normally we don't notice it, but I never thought it would be so inconvenient without electricity.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:38.010
A blackout with only this degree of snow. This is proof that they're neglecting their duties.

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.680
Get me their person in charge!

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:41.570
What will you do afterwards?

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:45.880
To prevent such things from happening again, I'm going to teach him a lesson!

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.690
Sounds good. You go and do that.

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:53.470
Wanna be teru teru bouzu?

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:54.400
Are you trying to kill me?!

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:57.490
Well, spending a night like this once in a while isn't so bad.

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:59.150
If it wasn't so cold, you mean.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.870
I wonder what everyone's doing.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.920
Oh, Fuyuki-kun.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:15.630
His father isn't home. I wonder if he's all right by himself.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.240
Want to go check?

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.880
Are you that worried about him?

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:24.120
If it's him, he should have a lot of good stuff.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:25.100
Let's go check.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:27.560
Okay.

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:35.090
Fuyuki, you there?

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:36.860
Hey, Fuyuki!

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.430
Maybe he went to sleep?

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:40.860
Children don't go to bed this early, right?

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:42.630
But he's an elementary student...

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:44.480
Well, that's true. Even so...

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:45.340
Haruka!

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:48.380
Maybe something strange happened?!

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:50.150
Something strange?

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:54.170
Hey, hey. He might have gone to sleep already.

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:55.840
No. He's still awake.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:01.490
Chiaki, that's enough. Let's go back.

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:02.340
Coming!

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:06.970
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.490
What's the matter, everyone?

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:14.410
It's nothing. We just thought we should help out each other as neighbors.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:17.070
Are you okay there, Fuyuki-kun?

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:18.840
Yes, I'm all right.

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:23.160
Since you didn't answer the door, I thought you were dead.

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:26.650
Enough with the tasteless jokes.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:29.450
We were just wondering what you were doing alone.

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:32.720
If you were here, why didn't you answer right away?

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:35.920
I'm sorry. I was just about to go to sleep.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:38.920
In those clothes?

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:42.930
Yes, I was about to get changed.

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:47.300
Fuyuki! Can we borrow a gas tank?

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.380
Yes, just a second please.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.820
Here, please take these.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:15:58.860
Thanks!

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:03.670
Oh? You even included pocket warmers. How thoughtful of you.

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:04.820
It's really cold after all.

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:07.590
You're such a nice guy!

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:08.530
Thank you.

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:12.370
Oh right, Fuyuki-kun. Do you want to come over to our place?

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:16.330
Oh, good idea. We can light up the stove now.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.080
Come on!

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:20.440
Um... I don't think that's...

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:23.370
Why not? No need to hold back.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.980
Let's talk through the night.

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:28.300
Why won't you come along?

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:29.700
But...

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:32.420
You have nothing to do anyway! Just come!

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:36.390
Um... I don't know when my father will be back.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:41.190
He'll be worried if he doesn't find me at home on such a snowy day.

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:43.900
I see... then it can't be helped.

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:46.950
When he actually wants to come...

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.040
See ya.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.450
Good night.

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:51.990
What a nice kid.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:54.600
Yeah, it looks like he'll be fine by himself.

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:16.180
You idiot.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:22.070
Just as I thought.

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:23.230
W–What?

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:26.150
Come.

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:29.820
What the-? Wait!

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:32.080
Let me go!

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.340
Um... what's wrong all of a sudden?

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.290
Do you not want to come over that much?

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:42.210
No... that's not it. It's because my father would worry–

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:46.210
Aren't you just making up excuses to turn us down while you're thinking?

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:49.090
There's no such thing.

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:51.000
If you want to come, then come.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.720
Why can't you be honest with yourself?

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:55.640
That's not true. I'm not...

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:58.310
Just looking at you annoys me to no end.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:03.140
If that's the case, then leave me alone.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.160
Huh?

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:08.570
If you've got something to say, then say it!

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:12.780
Why must you...

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.160
What's wrong? Spit it out!

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:19.040
I'm saying why must you talk to me like that?!

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:21.330
Take this!

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:23.010
Ouch.

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:24.830
H–Hold it!

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:26.840
Take this!

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:29.040
Damn you!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:32.830
Take this!

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:56.660
Um... wait, Kana-san?

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:59.020
What're you doing?

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:00.160
Let us join you guys.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:06.980
Here we come, you two!

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:08.670
We won't show any mercy!

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:12.130
Why do I have to team up with this guy?

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:14.470
A–Are you all right?

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:18.180
Don't worry about me. Fire back at them!

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:24.240
Take this!

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:27.980
At this rate, there's no way we can fight back.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:31.220
It's obviously impossible with this team combination.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:35.020
Okay, I'll do the throwing. You go make some snowballs.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:36.490
Got it!

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:38.450
Take that!

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:42.290
Hey, are they ready yet?

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:43.870
My hands are getting numb.

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:47.460
Here I come!

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:49.930
Hey, retreat!

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:51.000
Why?!

00:19:56.950 --> 00:20:00.360
It feels so much warmer with a flame.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.930
Thank you, convenience of civilization!

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:06.060
This is all thanks to Fuyuki-kun.

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:09.690
It's nothing. I think it's about time I head back.

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:12.590
Well, since you're here anyway, why don't you spend the night?

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:16.060
Okay.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:28.030
It feels so warm like this.

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:31.960
Yeah, we wouldn't be doing this if it wasn't for the blackout.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:34.930
We should have done this from the start.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:39.140
So warm...

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:41.390
Did you say something?

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:44.620
Eh? No, nothing.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:08.370
Good morning, Haruka-neesama.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:11.310
Morning. Looks like the power's back.

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:15.530
Where did Fuyuki-kun go?

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:16.300
Eh?

00:21:19.390 --> 00:21:20.460
That guy...

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:25.590
Hey, Fuyuki! You there?

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:26.770
Morning!

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:28.590
Fuyuki!

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:40.660
What is that guy doing?

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:43.360
Oh, Fuyuki is shoveling snow.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:45.790
How admirable!

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:58.170
That's just the way you are.

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:32.850
A cat's paw pad feels so comfy when you touch it.

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:35.950
Apparently the softness of it depends on a cat's living environment.

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:39.750
The paw pads of cats that spend most of their time outside are rougher because they constantly walk on solid ground.

00:23:39.750 --> 00:23:42.310
Whereas the ones of housecats are all soft and squishy.

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:44.730
All right, let's try comparing paw pads next time.
